<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cloud provisioning manifest overlay.
  Merged with higher priority than src/main when -Pcloudprovi is set.

  This is the APK the cloud serves to the Android setup wizard during QR Device Owner
  provisioning, so it is installed from a download URL rather than from Play. Play
  Protect blocks a sideloaded install outright when the app declares any of four
  permissions - RECEIVE_SMS, READ_SMS, a notification listener, or an accessibility
  service - with "App blocked to protect your device / This app can request access to
  sensitive data". A tester hit exactly that on a factory-reset tablet, mid-wizard,
  with no way past it. We declare the fourth one.

  So this overlay strips the AccessibilityService, and nothing else: unlike the Play
  Store build, a provisioning APK still needs REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES to self-update
  and to install managed apps silently.

  What that costs, on these devices only: screenshots of an *external* app in the
  foreground, and remote key injection into one. Everything else has another path -
  PixelCopy captures FreeKiosk's own window, dpm.lockNow() turns the screen off for a
  Device Owner, and setPermittedAccessibilityServices governs *other* apps' services
  and needs nothing of ours.

  The cost is small in practice because a QR-provisioned device cannot enable the
  service anyway: writing Settings.Secure needs WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS, which is not
  grantable to a Device Owner and only ever arrives through
  `adb shell pm grant com.freekiosk android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS` (see
  CHANGELOG #99). There is no ADB in a QR flow. Keep building with plain
  `assembleRelease` for ADB provisioning, where the service does work.

  Removing this does NOT guarantee provisioning succeeds: Play Protect also keeps an
  allowlist of approved DPCs, a separate axis on which overlays and silent installs
  also weigh. Verify on hardware before telling anyone it is fixed.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <application>
        <!-- Strip AccessibilityService (BIND_ACCESSIBILITY_SERVICE) -->
        <service
            android:name="com.freekiosk.FreeKioskAccessibilityService"
            tools:node="remove" />
    </application>

</manifest>
